      "updated_at": "2023-12-06T16:24:03Z",
      "body": "I'm actually a bit surprised that you haven't had to rewrite the whole libcrypto\\<->provider interface, or libcrypto's use of it.  After all, all provided functions are being declared as `(void (*)(void))` by the `OSSL_DISPATCH` structure, and are then cast to whatever function signature they really have when populating the diverse method structures in libcrypto.  That would be a huge potential case for a need of thunking, no?  Or have I misunderstood the issue?\r\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
